abstract: "A zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 development of 16 statements (19 audited exports, 884 declarations exhaustively axiom-audited via Lean.collectAxioms, 10 adversarial false-variant and hypothesis-necessity refutations, verified across six formal kernels in CI), with Rust, ISO C11 (ASan/UBSan + 7-law fuzzing + 7-law libFuzzer), and Python programs for the finite data. Formalizes the Haag-Kertzer-Rickards-Stange square obstruction for three Apollonian packings, the general d-dimensional Soddy-Gosset integrality dichotomy (LMW 2002), universal Abelian sandpile confluence and finite termination on sinked dissipative graphs, direct 9x9 Z^2 and A_2 Laplacian determinants and Dhar traces, an elementary triangular-lattice parity lemma, Markov's classical descent theorem combined with Ying Zhang's (2007) even mod-32 theorem for all positive Markov solutions, 5-step Markov quiver exchange identities, and Hurwitz's (1907) complete n=4 Vieta-orbit classification. No open problem is solved."
